.TH CTBREC-PORTRAITS 1 "2026-10-20" "ctbrec-portraits" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ctbrec-portraits \- extract model names and portrait images from a ctbrec models file
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ctbrec-portraits
[\fIOPTIONS\fP]
\fIFILE\fP
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ctbrec-portraits
reads a ctbrec (camrec) model database and writes one image per model,
named after the model.
.P
The database is a single JSON document with four top-level keys:
.B models
(the model list, with
.B name
and
.B url
for each entry),
.BR notes ,
.B portraits
and
.BR groups .
Each portrait entry holds the image as a base64 string in its
.B data
field plus the model
.B url
it belongs to; the encoding is usually JPEG, without a
.B data:
prefix. The portrait URL is the only link back to a model, so the script
joins it against
.B models[*].url
to recover the name. If a URL is not found in the model list, the last path
segment of the URL is used instead.
.P
The file extension is chosen from the decoded image's magic bytes
(JPEG, PNG, GIF, BMP, WebP); anything else is written as
.BR .bin .
Existing files are left alone unless
.B \-\-force
is given, so re-running the script is cheap and safe. Files that would
collide inside one run get a
.B \-2
style suffix.
.P
The whole file is parsed with the Python standard library; no network access
and no external programs are used. A database of a few megabytes parses
instantly.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-o ", " \-\-out " DIR"
Write images to
.IR DIR .
Default: the input file's own name with
.B \-portraits
appended, next to the input file, e.g.\&
.I models-portraits
for
.IR models .
.TP
.BI \-l ", " \-\-list
Print
.IR name ,
.IR filename ,
.IR url
and byte size for every portrait as tab-separated text, and write nothing.
.TP
.BI \-f ", " \-\-force
Overwrite images that already exist.
.TP
.BI \-m ", " \-\-manifest " PATH
Also write a TSV manifest with the header
.BR "name url file bytes" .
.TP
.BI \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Print the full list of models that have no portrait, rather than the first
ten.
.SH BEHAVIOUR
.SS Output
.IP \(bu 2
One image per portrait, named after the model: a portrait whose URL is
.I https://chaturbate.com/keix_moon/
is written as
.IR keix_moon.jpg .
.IP \(bu 2
Names are reduced to
.BR [A-Za-z0-9._-] ;
other characters become underscores.
.IP \(bu 2
A summary line reports how many images were written, skipped and failed, the
total size, and the output directory.
.IP \(bu 2
Models present in the model list but without a portrait are counted and
named at the end; they produce no file.
.SS Errors
.IP \(bu 2
A portrait with missing or undecodable base64 data is reported on standard
error and counted as failed; the rest of the file is still processed.
.IP \(bu 2
Unreadable or invalid JSON is fatal.
.SH EXAMPLES
Extract into
.IR models-portraits
next to the database:
.IP
.EX
ctbrec-portraits ~/Documents/models
.EE
.P
Extract somewhere else with a manifest:
.IP
.EX
ctbrec-portraits \-o ~/Pictures/ctbrec \-m ~/Pictures/ctbrec/index.tsv ~/Documents/models
.EE
.P
See the names and URLs without writing any files:
.IP
.EX
ctbrec-portraits \-\-list ~/Documents/models
.EE
.P
Refresh every image in place:
.IP
.EX
ctbrec-portraits \-\-force \-o ~/Pictures/ctbrec ~/Documents/models
.EE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success, including runs where some files were skipped because they already
existed.
.TP
.B 1
One or more portraits could not be written or decoded.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ctbrec-merge (1),
.BR ctbrec-vr (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Written for local use.
